  - [1mEllipsis appended on top[0m — same call → [38;5;153m"abcde..."[39m. Simpler to implement and to explain, no tiny-limit edge case, but
    the output can be 3 chars over the stated max, so it can't be used to guarantee a width.

  [1mMy recommendation:[0m ellipsis inside the budget. The whole point of a max length is a bound you can rely on, and the
  tiny-[38;5;153mmaxLength[39m case is one clamp, not real complexity.
